message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "PCA-τ with ANOVA/FDR Rescue"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Cuesta"
    given-names: "Jordi"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-3527-4836"

version: "1.0.0"

repository-code: "https://github.com/jordicuestand/pca-tau-anova-fdr-rescue"

license: "MIT"

keywords:
  - principal component analysis
  - feature selection
  - dimensionality reduction
  - ANOVA
  - false discovery rate
  - support vector machine
  - machine learning
  - low-variance components

abstract: >
  Reproducibility code accompanying the paper "PCA-τ with ANOVA/FDR Rescue".
  The HYBRID method preserves the variance-based PCA core and applies
  ANOVA with Benjamini-Hochberg false-discovery-rate correction only
  to discarded tail principal components, selectively rescuing those
  showing evidence of class discrimination.
